    "description": "Simulated 40m x 25m warehouse floor for the sim-driven demo (STATUS.md Step 2). Four camera zones (node 0..3), each an 8m-wide north-south column with racking-aisle obstacles inside it. Node 0's zone (x in [0, 8]) and node 1's zone (x in [11, 19]) flank a deliberate 3m-wide blind aisle (x in [8, 11]) that spans the full 25m depth of the floor — the C3/C4 demo apparatus this floor plan exists for. Its two exits are boundary_id 1 (x=8, node 0's side) and boundary_id 2 (x=11, node 1's side); a worker crossing either one while under that node's camera produces the coverage attestation the 'could be here' region shrinks against. Node 2 (x in [24, 32]) and node 3 (x in [35, 40]) cover two further zones with their own racking; the strips x in [19, 24] and x in [32, 35] are plain uncovered floor (no boundary instrumented there) — camera coverage deliberately does not span the whole building, matching the real deployment this demo represents."
